# AprilTag plate for the simulated dock — a single textured quad.
#
# WHY A MESH AND NOT AN SDF <box>: a box visual in gz-sim gets the material on
# every face with per-face UVs this file cannot control, and AprilTag detection
# is invariant to ROTATION but NOT to MIRRORING. A mirrored tag does not decode
# as a different id — it does not decode at all, and the failure looks exactly
# like "the detector isn't working". An explicit quad with authored UVs removes
# that guesswork.
#
# GEOMETRY: 0.125 m square, in the Y-Z plane, facing +X (normal 1 0 0).
#
# The 0.125 is not arbitrary. apriltag-imgs' tag36h11 PNGs are 10x10 px: a 6x6
# data grid, plus a 1-cell BLACK border (making 8x8), plus a 1-cell white quiet
# zone (making 10x10). apriltag_node's `size` parameter is the edge length of
# the BLACK BORDER, not of the image. So:
#
#     0.125 m plate x (8/10) = 0.100 m black border
#
# which is exactly docking.yaml's `size: 0.10`. Change one and you must change
# the other, or every pose is scaled wrong while the tag still detects — the
# quiet failure that parameter is famous for.
#
# WINDING / UV: the face is wound v1,v4,v3,v2 — NOT v1,v2,v3,v4 in plain
# declaration order — because that is what comes out CCW as seen from +X.
# Renderers backface-cull on the GEOMETRIC winding, not on the declared `vn`:
# an OBJ can assert vn = (1,0,0) and still be invisible from +X if the
# triangle order traces clockwise from that side. Verified the hard way on
# 2026-09-23 — the plain-order face rendered the dock's backing box but the
# tag itself was culled from exactly the direction the docking camera
# approaches from, which looked identical to a missing texture.
#
# Looking along -X with +Z up, screen-right is +Y (camera basis: Z_cam=+X,
# Y_cam=+Z, so X_cam = Y_cam x Z_cam = +Y). So the vertex at y=+h is on the
# image's RIGHT, and gets u=1. v=0 is the BOTTOM of the image.
#
# THE U COLUMN IS NOT ARBITRARY AND WAS WRONG ONCE. An earlier version assumed
# screen-right was -Y, which swapped u and rendered the tag MIRRORED. It looked
# perfect to the eye at any distance and never decoded, because AprilTag
# tolerates rotation but NOT mirroring. Caught 2026-09-23 by extracting the
# rendered 10x10 cell grid from a captured frame and matching it against the
# source PNG under all 8 dihedral transforms: np.fliplr matched at 1.000.
# If you touch these UVs, re-run that check — the eye cannot do it.
#
# IF THE TAG IS NEVER DETECTED IN SIM, suspect mirroring before anything else —
# flip the committed texture horizontally and restart Gazebo:
#   convert tag36h11_00000.png -flop tag36h11_00000.png
# That is a 30-second check, and it rules out the one convention this file
# cannot verify without a renderer. If it fixes it, commit the flipped PNG.

mtllib apriltag_plate.mtl
o apriltag_plate
usemtl tag

v 0.0  0.0625 -0.0625
v 0.0 -0.0625 -0.0625
v 0.0 -0.0625  0.0625
v 0.0  0.0625  0.0625

vt 1.0 0.0
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 0.0 1.0
vt 1.0 1.0

vn 1.0 0.0 0.0

f 1/1/1 4/4/1 3/3/1 2/2/1
